# Icons, states & loading (default — never remove)

These are **locked general rules**. Do not delete, skip, or replace with one-off patterns.

## Icon system (choose at install)

At intake, set Project Profile **Icons** to exactly one primary system:

| Choice | Use |
|--------|-----|
| **Material Icons** | Static Material Symbols / Material Icons for product chrome |
| **Lottie** | Animated icons via **Lottie web** JSON (`.json` / `.lottie`) for chrome and state screens |

Rules:

- One primary system per project (record in Profile + `frontend-design` skill)
- If **Lottie**: use official Lottie web player for the stack; store assets under a shared path (e.g. `public/lottie/` or `src/assets/lottie/`); prefer lightweight loops
- If **Material**: do not mix a second static icon library for chrome (emoji is not product chrome)
- Icon-only controls still need accessible names (`aria-label` / visible text)
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`: pause/stop Lottie loops or show a static frame

## Default state screens (required)

Ship shared, reusable screens/components — not ad-hoc per page:

| State | Required |
|-------|----------|
| **404** Not found | Animated/illustrated default page (route catch-all) |
| **Other status errors** | Shared error page/panel for 403, 500, offline, generic failure (status + message + recovery CTA when useful) |
| **Empty data** | Shared empty state for lists/tables/search with optional action |

Prefer Lottie (or the chosen icon system) for these animations so they match brand motion. Copy and CTAs follow project tokens — not bare browser defaults.

## Skeleton loaders (required)

- List, detail, dashboard, and other async content regions use **skeleton loaders** while loading
- Skeletons match layout shape (not a lone spinner unless the surface is tiny)
- Shared skeleton primitives in `components/ui/` (or equivalent)

## Lazy load (required)

- Route-level **lazy loading** for feature screens/chunks
- Lazy-load heavy media / below-fold images where the stack supports it
- Lottie players and large animations load on demand when practical (do not block first paint)

## Do not

- Skip 404 / error / empty defaults “until later”
- Replace skeletons with blank screens or only spinners for primary content
- Eager-load every route/chunk when lazy load is available
- Swap the locked icon system mid-project without updating Profile + skill
- Mix Material + another static icon set for the same chrome layer (Lottie may animate states even when Material is primary chrome — note that in Profile if hybrid)
